    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nNothing much just added a glyph for the \r\n`norg` filetype :)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/36cb3cf1-48d1-4036-9e35-e0d69ea5b02e)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-12-29T12:10:33Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI've merged in a separate branch to reword the commit message slightly. Should be merged by the end of the day into `main`.\r\n\r\n**Edit**: ~Oh... Although on closer inspection, this is an icon from 'devicons' set (i.e. `nf-dev-norg`). 'mini.icons' doesn't use glyphs from that set for consistency reasons. Sorry, not using 'nf-dev-norg' was intentional and won't be merged into `main`.~\r\nOn the third thought, 'neorg' is a Neovim-first project, so deserves a special treatment. Plus, [`nf-dev-*` glyphs *are* allowed](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2faada1cffce5609d78ac5e81eaf3754e0476758/lua/mini/icons.lua#L917), it is just `nf-md-*` should be preferred and used as the main reference.\r\n\r\nOne problem I had is that this glyph needs a fairly recent Nerd Font version: the one from around the middle of the summer didn't have this glyph, for example; updating to latest helped.",
