        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> On the third thought, 'neorg' is a Neovim-first project, so deserves a special treatment. Plus, [nf-dev-* glyphs are allowed](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2faada1cffce5609d78ac5e81eaf3754e0476758/lua/mini/icons.lua#L917), it is just nf-md-* should be preferred and used as the main reference.\r\n\r\nYayy!\r\n\r\n> One problem I had is that this glyph needs a fairly recent Nerd Font version: the one from around the middle of the summer didn't have this glyph, for example; updating to latest helped.\r\n\r\nValid point--But I believe most neorg users are likely using relatively up-to-date fonts and configurations.\r\n\r\nThanks for the detailed feedback.\r\n\r\n",
